Running sched_ext schedulers
===========================

Each scheduler has its own binary package and command in /usr/bin.
Commands retain their upstream names, for example scx_panda and
scx_pandemonium. This package installs the complete set. To retain an
individual scheduler after removing scx-full, mark it as manually installed
with apt-mark manual.

Run the selected command with --help to inspect its options. Loading a
scheduler requires an appropriately privileged process and a kernel with
sched_ext enabled. Check /sys/kernel/sched_ext/state and the selected
scheduler's manual for additional requirements. The kernel's scheduler
resumes control when the active sched_ext scheduler is detached.

Mitosis and Nitosis use cgroup-based configuration. Nitosis also requires
the sub_cid_sched_updated struct_ops callback from Linux 7.4 or a backport
that provides it.
